! ============================================================
! 01d  What else the wavefunction tells you
! ============================================================
! One energy, but with the property output switched on.
!
! WHAT TO LOOK AT:
!   * ORBITAL ENERGIES.  The HOMO energy is an estimate of
!     minus the ionization potential (Koopmans' theorem).
!     Here e_HOMO ~ -0.50 Eh = -13.6 eV against an experimental
!     IP of 12.6 eV -- a fair estimate, and it works because
!     two errors cancel: neglect of orbital relaxation (raises
!     it) and neglect of correlation (lowers it).
!   * the LUMO energy from HF is NOT an electron affinity;
!     with a diffuse basis it drifts towards zero.  Do not
!     read chemistry into it.
!   * POPULATION ANALYSIS.  Mulliken charges are basis-set
!     dependent -- run this with cc-pVTZ and watch them move
!     substantially while the dipole moment barely does.  The
!     dipole is an observable; a partial charge is not.
!   * DIPOLE MOMENT: ~2.2 D here against 1.85 D experimental.
!     HF overpolarizes.
%method  HF
%basis   6-31G(d)
%job     energy
%charge  0
%mult    1
%print_mo     on
%pop_analysis on

%geo
 O   0.0000000   0.0000000   0.1173000
 H   0.0000000   0.7572000  -0.4692000
 H   0.0000000  -0.7572000  -0.4692000
